Keras - deep learning framework
AlphaZero - a self-play reinforcement learning algorithm. It combines:
    - Neural Network:
        Policy head
        Value head
    - Monte Carlo Tree Search (uses neural network predictions to explore the game tree)
    - Self-Play + Training loop (the agent plays against itself using MCTS guided moves).
    The Neural Network is updated to better match outcomes

In Keras-based AlphaZero implementation, the Neural Network is built with Keras:
    - Input: board state (tensor)
    - Shared Layers: convolutions
    - Two Outputs:
        Policy head - probabilities over legal moves
        Value head - scalar game outcome (-1 loss, 0 draw, 1 win)

The Keras model provides:
    Policy priors (probabilities over moves)
    Value estimates (how good the position is)
The MCTS uses those priors + values to search the game tree more deeply

https://blog.paperspace.com/building-a-checkers-gaming-agent-using-neural-networks-and-reinforcement-learning/

